LEVEL6 {Auto Validator}

SYSMENU {<ESC>[1;36m
Auto Validator v<TV:GALAV_VERSION> - Sysop Menu

  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mS<ESC>[1;36m) Settings
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mE<ESC>[1;36m) Validation email (from, subject and body)
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mL<ESC>[1;36m) Look up a user
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mG<ESC>[1;36m) Show the sysop global commands
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m) Exit Auto Validator
} T Sysop main menu

SYSPRMPT {<ESC>[1;36m
<ESC>[1;32mAuto Validator Sysop Menu<ESC>[1;36m
Make your selection (<ESC>[1;37mS,E,L,G,? <ESC>[1;36mfor help, or <ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to exit): } T Sysop main menu prompt

SYSHELP {<ESC>[1;35m
...Auto Validator validates new users by email.  A user enters the
module, gives an email address, and is sent a code.  When they return
and enter the code, they are validated: switched to a new class, given
a key and/or posted credits, as set up for the validation method.

Settings changes made here take effect immediately.  Use Look up to
see a user's validation record, and the global commands to validate,
devalidate or re-send codes from anywhere on the system.
} T Sysop main menu help

SETMENU {<ESC>[1;36m
Auto Validator Settings (changes apply immediately)

  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mG<ESC>[1;36m) General settings
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37m1<ESC>[1;36m-<ESC>[1;37m5<ESC>[1;36m) Validation method 1-5 settings
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mR<ESC>[1;36m) Reset all settings to the defaults
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m) Return to the sysop menu
} T Settings menu

SETPRMPT {<ESC>[1;36m
<ESC>[1;32mSettings<ESC>[1;36m
Make your selection (<ESC>[1;37mG,1-5,R <ESC>[1;36mor <ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to go back): } T Settings menu prompt

SETHDR {<ESC>[1;36m
<ESC>[1;32m<TV:GALAV_PAGE><ESC>[1;34m
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
} T Header of a settings page

SETROW {<ESC>[1;36m  (<ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_ITEM:R:2><ESC>[1;36m) <TV:GALAV_LABEL:L:34> <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_VALUE>
} T One row of a settings page

SETPGPR {<ESC>[1;36m
Item number to change, or <ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to go back: } T Settings page prompt

SETVALPR {<ESC>[1;36m
<TV:GALAV_LABEL> is now: <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_VALUE><ESC>[1;36m
Allowed: <TV:GALAV_LIMIT>
New value (Enter keeps it, a single - clears it): } T Settings value prompt

SETSAVED {<ESC>[1;32m
<TV:GALAV_LABEL> set to: <TV:GALAV_VALUE>
} T Setting saved confirmation

SETBAD {<ESC>[1;31m
That value is not allowed.  Allowed: <TV:GALAV_LIMIT>
} T Invalid setting value

SETNOCLS {<ESC>[1;31m
There is no class named "<TV:GALAV_VALUE>" in your Accounts setup.
Create the class first, then set it here.
} T Class name for a method does not exist

SETRSTQ {<ESC>[1;31m
This replaces ALL Auto Validator settings with the default values.
Are you sure (Y/N)? } T Reset settings confirmation

SETRSTD {<ESC>[1;32m
All settings were reset to the defaults.
} T Settings reset confirmation

EMLMENU {<ESC>[1;36m
Validation Email

  Sent from... <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_FROM><ESC>[1;36m
  Subject..... <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_SUBJECT><ESC>[1;36m
  Body........ <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_BODYSRC><ESC>[1;36m

  The From address is a setting (Settings, General).  In the subject
  and body, [NAME] is replaced by the text variable NAME when the email
  is sent:
    <ESC>[1;37m[GALAV_USERID]<ESC>[1;36m the User-ID    <ESC>[1;37m[GALAV_CODE]<ESC>[1;36m  the validation code
    <ESC>[1;37m[GALAV_EMAIL]<ESC>[1;36m  the address    <ESC>[1;37m[SYSTEM_NAME]<ESC>[1;36m your system's name

  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mE<ESC>[1;36m) Edit the subject and body
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mR<ESC>[1;36m) Restore the default subject and body
  <ESC>[1;36m(<ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m) Return to the sysop menu
} T Validation email menu

EMLPRMPT {<ESC>[1;36m
<ESC>[1;32mValidation Email<ESC>[1;36m
Make your selection (<ESC>[1;37mE,R <ESC>[1;36mor <ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to go back): } T Validation email menu prompt

EMLSAVED {<ESC>[1;32m
The validation email was saved.  It is used from the next email sent.
} T Validation email saved after editing

EMLKEPT {<ESC>[1;36m
Editing abandoned.  The validation email was not changed.
} T Validation email editing abandoned

EMLWRERR {<ESC>[1;31m
The body could not be written to GALAVEML.TXT.  Check the disk and the
file's permissions in the BBS directory.
} T Validation email body could not be saved

EMLRSTQ {<ESC>[1;31m
This replaces the validation email subject with the default subject
and the body with the default text (YOUVAL).  Are you sure (Y/N)? } T Restore default email confirmation

EMLRSTD {<ESC>[1;32m
The default validation email subject and body were restored.
} T Default email restored

LKUPPR {<ESC>[1;36m
User-ID to look up (or <ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to go back): } T Sysop user lookup prompt

USERINFO {<ESC>[1;36m
Auto Validator record for <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_USERID><ESC>[1;36m

  Email address....... <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_EMAIL><ESC>[1;36m
  Validated........... <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_VALID><ESC>[1;36m
  Pending code........ <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_CODE><ESC>[1;36m
  Validation method... <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_METHOD><ESC>[1;36m
  Failed attempts..... <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_ATTEMPTS><ESC>[1;36m
  Override............ <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_OVERRIDE><ESC>[1;36m
  Validated users sharing this email: <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_COUNT><ESC>[1;36m
} T Sysop view of a user's validation record

AUTOQURY {<ESC>[1;36m
Your account is not validated yet.  Would you like to validate it now (Y/N)? } T Logon offer to validate

ALRDYVLD {<ESC>[1;31m
The Auto Validator is for new users only.  Exiting Auto Validator.
} T User lacks the key needed to request validation

POSTVALD {<ESC>[1;35m
Your account has already been validated.  Email your Sysop if you
believe this is a mistake.
} T User is already validated

TOMNYVLD {<ESC>[1;31m
There have been too many unsuccessful attempts to validate your account.
Contact the Sysop if you still wish to be validated.
} T User has used up their validation attempts

CNTEMAIL {<ESC>[1;31m
Too many users are already validated with that <TV:GALAV_EMAILTYP> email
address.  You cannot be validated with it.  Contact your Sysop if you
still wish to be validated.
} T Email address already used by too many validated users

EMALCONT {<ESC>[1;36m
To validate your account, a validation code will be sent to your
<TV:GALAV_EMAILTYP> email address along with your User-ID.  When the email
arrives, return to the Auto Validator and enter the code.  You will
then be a validated user of <TV:SYSTEM_NAME>.

Do you wish to begin email validation now (Y/N)? } T Offer to start email validation

COMEBACK {<ESC>[1;36m
Return whenever you are ready to be validated.
} T User declined to validate now

EMALQURY {<ESC>[1;36m
Please enter your email address (<ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to abort): } T Email address prompt

OOPSQURY {<ESC>[1;31m
That does not look like a valid email address.
<ESC>[1;36mPlease enter it in the form name@example.com (<ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to abort): } T Malformed email address

EMAILNO {<ESC>[1;31m
Sorry, validation codes cannot be sent to that address.  Please use
an address on another system.
<ESC>[1;36mPlease enter your email address (<ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to abort): } T Email address refused by BADEMAIL or GALAVBAD.TXT

MAILSENT {<ESC>[1;32m
Your validation code has been sent to <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_EMAIL><ESC>[1;32m.
When it arrives, return to the Auto Validator and enter the code.
} T Validation email sent

SENDFAIL {<ESC>[1;31m
The validation email could not be sent.  Please try again later, or
contact the Sysop.
} T Validation email could not be sent

MAILQURY {<ESC>[1;36m
A validation code was emailed to <ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_EMAIL><ESC>[1;36m.
Please enter the code (<ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to exit): } T Ask for the emailed code

MISTYPE {<ESC>[1;31m
That code does not match.  Perhaps you mistyped it?
<ESC>[1;36mPlease enter the code (<ESC>[1;37mX<ESC>[1;36m to exit): } T Wrong code entered

SORRY {<ESC>[1;31m
That code still does not match.  Please email the Sysop about this
problem.  Sorry for the inconvenience.
} T Third wrong code in one visit

ABORTCDE {<ESC>[1;36m
Validation aborted.  Return when you have your code.
} T User left the code prompt

LATER {<ESC>[1;32m
You are now a validated member of <TV:SYSTEM_NAME>.  Have a nice day!
} T Validation succeeded

ADDCRDT {<ESC>[1;32m
<TV:GALAV_CREDITS> credits have been posted to your account.
} T Credits posted on validation

VALIDERR {<ESC>[1;31m
Your account could not be fully validated because of a setup problem.
The Sysop has been notified.
} T Method class missing at validation time

YOUVAL {
Greetings!

This message was sent to you from <TV:SYSTEM_NAME> because you asked to
validate your account there.

Call <TV:SYSTEM_NAME> again, log on with your User-ID, and go to the Auto
Validator.  It will ask for your validation code (below).  Enter it and
you are all set.

    Your User-ID is: <TV:GALAV_USERID>
    Your code is:    <TV:GALAV_CODE>

We hope you enjoy our system.  If you have any questions, please do not
hesitate to ask!
} T Default body of the validation email (plain text)

GLBLCMND {<ESC>[1;36m
  Auto Validator Global Commands:

<ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_GLOB>V (method) (user)<ESC>[1;36m.. Validate a user with method 1-5.
                       Example: <TV:GALAV_GLOB>V 1 Some User
<ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_GLOB>D (user)<ESC>[1;36m........... Devalidate: clear validation and attempts so
                       the user can validate again.
<ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_GLOB>E (user)<ESC>[1;36m........... Email the user their code again.
<ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_GLOB>L (user)<ESC>[1;36m........... Look up a user's validation record.
<ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_GLOB>O (user)<ESC>[1;36m........... Toggle the override (ignores attempt and
                       email limits).
<ESC>[1;37m<TV:GALAV_GLOB>?<ESC>[1;36m.................. Show this list.
} T Sysop global command list

BADGLOB {<ESC>[1;31m
That is not a valid Auto Validator command.  Type <TV:GALAV_GLOB>? for the list.
} T Unknown or incomplete global command

WRNGSNTX {<ESC>[1;31m
The format is: <TV:GALAV_GLOB>V (method 1-5) (user)
} T Bad format for the validate command

DVALSNTX {<ESC>[1;31m
The format is: <TV:GALAV_GLOB>D (user)
} T Bad format for the devalidate command

EMALSNTX {<ESC>[1;31m
The format is: <TV:GALAV_GLOB>E (user)
} T Bad format for the email command

OVERSNTX {<ESC>[1;31m
The format is: <TV:GALAV_GLOB>O (user)
} T Bad format for the override command

LKUPSNTX {<ESC>[1;31m
The format is: <TV:GALAV_GLOB>L (user)
} T Bad format for the look up command

NOUSER {<ESC>[1;31m
There is no user "<TV:GALAV_USERID>" on this system.
} T User-ID not found

NOAVREC {<ESC>[1;31m
"<TV:GALAV_USERID>" has never used the Auto Validator.
} T User has no Auto Validator record

NOEMAIL {<ESC>[1;31m
<TV:GALAV_USERID> has not given an email address.  Nothing was sent.
} T Resend email for a user with no address

FORCE {<ESC>[1;32m
<TV:GALAV_USERID> has been validated with method <TV:GALAV_METHOD>.
} T Forced validation confirmation

DEVAL {<ESC>[1;32m
<TV:GALAV_USERID> has been devalidated and may now validate again.
} T Devalidate confirmation

OVERRIDE {<ESC>[1;32m
The override for <TV:GALAV_USERID> is now <TV:GALAV_OVERRIDE>.
} T Override toggle confirmation

RESENT {<ESC>[1;32m
The validation code was emailed to <TV:GALAV_USERID> at <TV:GALAV_EMAIL>.
} T Code resent by the sysop

FSENDBAD {<ESC>[1;31m
The email to <TV:GALAV_USERID> could not be sent.  Check your Internet
mail settings and the EMAILPFX setting.
} T Sysop resend failed
